WEBVTT

00:00:01.024 --> 00:00:03.440
The system would enrich the

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.960
prospect, it would research,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.960
it goes to each prospect,

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.850
it does a complete research,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.320
tells us why this person

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.650
may be relevant for us,

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.460
gives us the signals and

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.140
the outreach angles that we

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.180
can do.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.350
Now the emails

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.620
are being generated by the

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.360
system based on the research

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.500
and based on what it

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.790
learned about your service

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.750
and it creates the emails.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.100
And it could either be

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.960
when a user fills up

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.280
a form on your website

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.640
and then the voice agent

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.262
immediately calls him.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:38.780
Thanks for calling

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.640
MeetingScheduled.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.820
How can I help you

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.370
today?

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.640
MeetingScheduled builds digital

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.860
phone receptionists for

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.940
businesses, so your calls can

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.250
be answered automatically,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.640
even after hours or when

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.520
your team is busy.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.860
This is the Speed Dialer

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.840
app where you are able

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.760
to call, email,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.690
WhatsApp, look at the company.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.260
once I do the call

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.340
I'm able to see my

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.210
recent calls you

00:01:02.784 --> 00:01:04.160
download them to see the

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.060
transcript of each one When

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.100
we click on one of

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.910
the leads we've spoken with,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.330
we can hear the recordings.

00:01:14.304 --> 00:01:15.540
We can see the transcript

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.630
directly here,
